module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FinGenFromCover.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleAffineAvoidance.Powers

/-!
# One tensor power of an ample module is generated by finitely many global sections

This file closes the first of the two missing inputs recorded under "What is not done" in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/AmpleEventualGeneration/Basic.lean`: for an ample invertible
`𝒪_X`-module `L` there is a `d ≥ 1` with `L ^⊗ d` generated by finitely many global sections.
That is the first sentence of the source's construction of `n₀(L)` in [Stacks, Tag 01Q3] —
"choose finitely many `s_i ∈ S_{d_i}` with `X = ⋃ X_{s_i}`, put `d = d_1 ⋯ d_n`, then `L ^⊗ d` is
globally generated by `s_1^{d/d_1}, …, s_n^{d/d_n}`".

## The route, in four steps

1. **Ampleness gives a pointwise cover.** `Stacks.Ample.IsAmpleForPowers` says each `x` lies in
   `X_s` for a global section `s` of some positive power; `IsAffineOpen` is discarded here, since
   nothing below uses it.
2. **Change of vocabulary.** `Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.exists_powSections_nvLocus_eq` turns
   each such `s` into a homogeneous element of the section ring with the same nonvanishing locus,
   which is the vocabulary in which the powers are available;
   `Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_global_nonvanishingLocus_eq` is the inverse passage, needed to
   get back to the `Γ(L ^⊗ d, ⊤)` that `Stacks.FinGenFromCover.isFinGen_of_nonvanishingCover`
   consumes.
3. **Quasi-compactness** — the first conjunct of ampleness — cuts the cover down to a finite
   subfamily, indexed by a `Finset` of points of `X`.
4. **One common degree.** `Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_common_degree_family` replaces the whole
   finite family by powers of a single degree.

## Why the degree equalisation needs no induction

`Stacks.AmpleAffineAvoidance.exists_common_degree` equalises **two** degrees, by passing to the
common degree `d n`. The `n`-fold version is sometimes expected to be an induction over a
`Finset`; it is not. Take the degree to be `∏ i, n i` over `Finset.univ`: each `n i` divides it by
`Finset.dvd_prod_of_mem`, the product is positive because every factor is, and
`Stacks.AmpleAffineAvoidance.exists_pow_of_dvd` — "a homogeneous element has a power in every
positive degree it divides, with the same nonvanishing locus" — then applies to every member
independently. The whole proof is `choose` over that one application, with no recursion and no
transport, because `exists_pow_of_dvd` already absorbed the arithmetic of `n * (k + 1)`.

The hypothesis is `Finite ι` rather than `Fintype ι`: the conclusion is existential, so the
`Fintype` instance the product needs is manufactured inside the proof by `Fintype.ofFinite` and
never appears in the statement.

## Main results

* `Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_common_degree_family`: **a finite family of homogeneous elements
  of positive degrees has powers of one common degree**, with the original nonvanishing loci. The
  `n`-fold generalisation of `Stacks.AmpleAffineAvoidance.exists_common_degree`.
* `Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_global_nonvanishingLocus_eq`: the inverse of the vocabulary
  bridge — a homogeneous element of degree `n` is an honest global section of `L ^⊗ n` with the
  same nonvanishing locus.
* `Stacks.FinGenFromCover.isOpen_nvLocus`: `X_s` is open, in the section-ring vocabulary.
* `Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_pos_isFinGen_tensorPowModule`: **the deliverable.** For `L`
  ample there is a `d ≥ 1` with `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen (L ^⊗ d)`.
* `Stacks.FinGenFromCover.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_clauseFive`: half (1) of clause (7) of
  [Stacks, Tag 01Q3] for an ample `L`, **on the one remaining hypothesis**, stated in the source's
  own shape — clause (5) of Tag 01Q3 for the sheaf `L ^⊗ d` applied to `F = L ^⊗ j`. This is the
  precise residual, and it is what Tag 01PW would discharge.

## Implementation notes

**The local monoidal instances are the exact list of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/AmpleAffineAvoidance/Powers.lean`**, for the same reason: the
section-ring vocabulary (`Stacks.GradedSections.powSections`,
`Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.nvLocus`) is stated for an abstract monoidal category, and the list
is what makes `X.Modules` one. It is a superset of the two instances that
`AmpleEventualGeneration/` installs, so the `⊗` of
`Stacks.FinGenFromCover.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_clauseFive` is the same monoidal product as
the one in `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_forall_exists_pow`.
`Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeSectionCommRing` is deliberately *not* installed; nothing here
mentions the ring structure of `Γ_*(X, L)`, only the degreewise product.

**The index of the finite cover is a subtype of a `Finset` of points.** `X` is a `Scheme.{u}`, so
`↥X : Type u` and `{y : ↥X // y ∈ F} : Type u`, which is the universe
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen` requires of a generating index. Reindexing by anything
smaller would need the cover to be deduplicated, which buys nothing.

No tag attribute is attached. Tag 01Q3 asserts the equivalence of all nine of its clauses, and
what is proved here is one of the two inputs to one half of one clause. Tag 01AN is the
stalkwise criterion itself, which is proved elsewhere and is not reproved here; see
`Stacks.FinGenFromCover.isFinGen_of_nonvanishingCover`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CV)

## What is not done

**Half (1) of clause (7) is still not proved from ampleness, and exactly one input remains.**
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsEventuallyFinGenPowers` asks for *every* sufficiently positive
degree; what ampleness alone yields is one positive degree `d`, hence — by
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.finGenDegrees_add` — every positive multiple of `d`, together with
degree `0`. Filling the other residue classes modulo `d` is the source's second use of clause (5),
and it is not available: `Stacks.FinGenFromCover.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_clauseFive` carries
it as a hypothesis. Clause (5) is stated nowhere in the repository and the source derives it from
[Stacks, Tag 01PW], which has no formalization anywhere in the tree. So the
`IsEventuallyFinGenPowers` half of what [Stacks, Tag 0EBD] and [Stacks, Tag 087S] owe is reduced
to Tag 01PW and nothing else.

**The degree `d` produced is not minimal and is not canonical.** It is the product of the degrees
appearing in one particular finite subcover, chosen through `Classical.choice` twice over (once
per point of `X`, once for the subcover), so no statement below determines it. The source's `d`
is the same product and is equally arbitrary; nothing downstream depends on which `d` it is,
because `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_forall_emod` quantifies over
the residue classes of whatever `d` it is handed.

**Affineness of the covering `X_s` is thrown away.** `Stacks.Ample.IsAmpleForPowers` provides it
and `exists_pos_isFinGen_tensorPowModule` discards it. It is not needed for global generation, and
a consumer that wants both must call ampleness again.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.Ample Stacks.GradedSections Stacks.SectionProduct Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance
open Stacks.AmpleAffineAvoidance

universe u

namespace Stacks.FinGenFromCover

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isMonoidal_localIso
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isLocalization_sheafify Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.sheafifyMonoidal Stacks.SheafInternalHom.braidedCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeBraidedCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemePreadditive
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeTensorRightAdditive

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (L : X.Modules) [IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-! ### A finite family of homogeneous elements in one common degree -/

/-- **A finite family of homogeneous elements of positive degrees has powers of a single common
degree**, with the original nonvanishing loci. The `n`-fold generalisation of
`Stacks.AmpleAffineAvoidance.exists_common_degree`, which does the case of two.

The common degree is `∏ i, n i`: every `n i` divides it, so
`Stacks.AmpleAffineAvoidance.exists_pow_of_dvd` applies to each member separately and no induction
is involved. -/
theorem exists_common_degree_family {ι : Type u} [Finite ι] (n : ι → ℕ) (hn : ∀ i, 1 ≤ n i)
    (a : (i : ι) → powSections L (n i)) :
    ∃ (m : ℕ) (a' : (i : ι) → powSections L m), 1 ≤ m ∧
      ∀ i, nvLocus L (a' i) = nvLocus L (a i) := by
  let _ := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  have hm : 1 ≤ ∏ i, n i := (Finset.prod_pos fun i _ => hn i : 0 < ∏ i, n i)
  choose a' ha' using fun i =>
    exists_pow_of_dvd L (a i) (Finset.dvd_prod_of_mem n (Finset.mem_univ i)) hm
  exact ⟨_, a', hm, ha'⟩

/-! ### Back from the section ring to honest global sections -/

/-- **The vocabulary bridge, read backwards.** A homogeneous element of degree `n` of the section
ring is an honest global section of `L ^⊗ n` with the same nonvanishing locus.
`Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.exists_powSections_nvLocus_eq` is the other direction. -/
theorem exists_global_nonvanishingLocus_eq (n : ℕ) (a : powSections L n) :
    ∃ s : Γ(tensorPowModule X L (n : ℤ), ⊤),
      nonvanishingLocus (tensorPowModule X L (n : ℤ)) s = nvLocus L a := by
  have heq : (Stacks.TensorPowers.natTensorPow L n : X.Modules) = tensorPowModule X L (n : ℤ) :=
    Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.natTensorPow_eq_tensorPow
      (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf X) L n
  let e : (Stacks.TensorPowers.natTensorPow L n : X.Modules) ≅ tensorPowModule X L (n : ℤ) :=
    eqToIso (C := X.Modules) heq
  exact ⟨e.hom.app ⊤ (globalSection X _ a), nonvanishingLocus_congr e _⟩

/-- `X_s` is open, in the section-ring vocabulary: it is the carrier of
`Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.nvOpen`. -/
theorem isOpen_nvLocus {n : ℕ} (a : powSections L n) : IsOpen (nvLocus L a) := by
  rw [← coe_nvOpen L a]
  exact (nvOpen L a).2

/-! ### One power of an ample module is generated by finitely many global sections -/

/-- **For an ample invertible `𝒪_X`-module there is a positive degree in which the tensor power is
generated by finitely many global sections.**

This is the first sentence of the source's construction of `n₀(L)` in [Stacks, Tag 01Q3]: a finite
subcover of the affine cover that ampleness provides, its degrees equalised to their product, and
the stalkwise criterion applied to the resulting family. -/
theorem exists_pos_isFinGen_tensorPowModule (hL : IsAmple X L) :
    ∃ d : ℕ, 1 ≤ d ∧ Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen (tensorPowModule X L (d : ℤ)) := by
  have := hL.compactSpace
  have hpt : ∀ x : X, ∃ (n : ℕ) (a : powSections L n), 1 ≤ n ∧ x ∈ nvLocus L a := by
    intro x
    obtain ⟨n, hn, s, U, hU, hxU, -⟩ :=
      IsAmpleForPowers.exists_affine_nonvanishingLocus (pow := tensorPowModule X L) hL x
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := exists_powSections_nvLocus_eq L n s
    exact ⟨n, a, hn, by rwa [ha, ← hU]⟩
  choose n a hn ha using hpt
  obtain ⟨F, hF⟩ := isCompact_univ.elim_finite_subcover (fun y : X => nvLocus L (a y))
    (fun y => isOpen_nvLocus L (a y)) fun x _ => Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨x, ha x⟩
  obtain ⟨d, b, hd, hb⟩ :=
    exists_common_degree_family L (ι := {y : X // y ∈ F}) (fun i => n i.1) (fun i => hn i.1)
      fun i => a i.1
  choose t ht using fun i : {y : X // y ∈ F} => exists_global_nonvanishingLocus_eq L d (b i)
  refine ⟨d, hd, isFinGen_of_nonvanishingCover _ t fun x => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨y, hy, hxy⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp (hF (Set.mem_univ x))
  exact ⟨⟨y, hy⟩, by rwa [ht ⟨y, hy⟩, hb ⟨y, hy⟩]⟩

/-- **Half (1) of clause (7) of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3] for an ample `L`, on the single remaining
hypothesis.** The hypothesis is clause (5) of Tag 01Q3 for the sheaf `L ^⊗ d`, applied to
`F = L ^⊗ j`: for every positive `d` and every `j` some tensor power of `L ^⊗ d` twists `L ^⊗ j`
into a module generated by finitely many global sections.

Ampleness supplies the other input, the one positive degree `d` of
`Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_pos_isFinGen_tensorPowModule`, and
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_forall_exists_pow` does the
residue-class bookkeeping. So this is the exact residual: clause (5), hence
[Stacks, Tag 01PW], and nothing else. -/
theorem isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_clauseFive (hL : IsAmple X L)
    (h : ∀ d : ℤ, 0 < d → ∀ j : ℤ, ∃ k : ℕ, Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen
      (tensorPowModule X L j ⊗ tensorPowModule X (tensorPowModule X L d) (k : ℤ))) :
    Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsEventuallyFinGenPowers X L := by
  obtain ⟨d, hd, hdgen⟩ := exists_pos_isFinGen_tensorPowModule L hL
  have hd' : (0 : ℤ) < (d : ℤ) := by exact_mod_cast hd
  exact Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_forall_exists_pow hd' hdgen
    (h (d : ℤ) hd')

end Stacks.FinGenFromCover

end
